{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "duo_corner_offdiag",
    "description": "PASS 1 of the duo corner fill: overwrite the 6 OFF-DIAGONAL points of each of the 4 corners by 1-D Lagrange extension of the adjacent edge lines (Zerroukat eqs 8-9). Bind q to the edge-filled halo (duo_extend output). Duo-grid CUBE-CORNER halo fill (Zerroukat & Allen 2021 QJRMS 10.1002/qj.4230; Mouallem 2023 fv_duogrid.F90 fill_corner_region_2d) for a cell-centred A-grid field, to cubic (order-4) accuracy, needed by TRULY 2-D (non-split) stencils -- the direction-split LMARS reconstructions never read the corner blocks, so duo_extend leaves them unfilled. Projection-agnostic: barycentric-Lagrange weights from GREAT-CIRCLE distances between cell centres (via the shared duo_arc_length atom), so equidistance/equiangular/equi-edge alike. Each corner's 3x3 halo block is one aggregate with an ifelse selecting the interpolation direction on the two off-diagonal triangles. TWO passes because the diagonal reads the just-filled off-diagonal. Bind center to duo_cell_center; R_sphere is a consumer free name. Verified bit-identical to a numeric reimplementation of the Fortran over all 4 corners; converges at ~4th order.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "grid:duo",
      "op:corner_fill",
      "order:4",
      "bc:duo",
      "axes:tile,x_cell_ext,y_cell_ext",
      "form:interp",
      "spec:9.6.8"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Zerroukat, M., & Allen, T. (2022). On the corners of the cubed-sphere grid. QJRMS, 148(743), 778-783."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Mouallem, J., Harris, L., & Chen, X. (2023). Implementation of the novel Duo-Grid in GFDL's FV3. JAMES, 15, e2023MS003712."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "../grid.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "../stencils/duo_arc_length.esm"
    }
  ],
